Overrides for desktop entries that should not appear in the launcher.

freedesktop resolves an entry by ID, and a file here replaces the one of the
same name under /usr/share/applications. Setting NoDisplay=true is how you
retire a system entry without editing a packaged file that the next upgrade
would put straight back.

What is buried here, and why:

  foot-server, footclient   Two more ways to reach the same terminal. Searching
                            "term" returned three near-identical results and
                            two of them do nothing useful started by hand.
  lstopo                    Draws a diagram of the CPU topology. It is a
                            dependency of the hardware tooling, not something
                            anyone opens on purpose.

The terminal itself stays: foot.desktop carries Keywords=terminal, which is
what makes searching "terminal" find it.
